# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HoneyBeeSMP monorepo
#
# The repo is the source of truth for things we author (website, bot, tooling).
# Excluded on purpose (large / regenerable / secret):
#   - Minecraft worlds, jars, libraries, mods  (~189M) -> backed up separately
#   - Crafty databases, TLS keys, admin creds          -> secrets, never commit
#   - Logs, caches, backups, runtime state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Symlinks to system paths -----------------------------------------------
# These point outside the repo (/opt/crafty, /var/www, ...). Git stores only
# the link target, never the contents, which is misleading. Tracked sources
# live under ./website and ./bot instead.
/crafty-panel
/minecraft-servers
/discord-bot

# --- Minecraft server data (backed up separately) ---------------------------
# These are the *installed* server files on the machine, not the config we
# author. The configuration we author lives in minecraft/ and IS tracked.
servers/
world/
world_nether/
world_the_end/
libraries/
*.jar
crash-reports/
# Mods are installed at runtime; we track the list in
# minecraft/mods/mods.manifest instead of the jar files themselves.
/mods/
# (but not our own minecraft/ directory)
!/minecraft/

# --- Crafty panel -----------------------------------------------------------
crafty/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.db
default-creds.txt
session.lock
*.pem
*.key

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Note the repo-root .env pattern is anchored so bot/.env.example survives.
/.env
/.env.*
!.env.example
bot/.env
bot/.env.*
!bot/.env.example
*.secret
*credential*

# --- Backups -----------------------------------------------------------------
backups/
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
*.bak

# --- Logs & caches ----------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
.cache/
tmp/
.tmp/

# --- Language / tooling -----------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
# A Python virtualenv is called "env" - but ours is minecraft/env, which
# holds per-environment server settings and must be tracked.
/env/
!/minecraft/env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# --- Editor / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# --- Local-only documentation ------------------------------------------------
# The internal runbook (hostnames, paths, credential locations) is kept out
# of the published repo on purpose. The README is the public document.
docs/OPERATIONS.md

# --- Runtime data -----------------------------------------------------------
data/
